|ا	|67	| Al Ahad	|الاحد	|The One, the Indivisible |
|ا	|73	| Al Awwal	|الأول	|The First |
|ا	|74	|Al Aakhir	|الآخر	|The Last|

# the ا #Alif
- alif; when it does not have the Hamza (ء)), in the middle of a word is silent which in this case represents the inactivity of the chrysalis which also looks very similar in shape to the letter ا

- ا are used to indicate vertical or tall structures

- ا is the growth (rather than movement since it is attached to the ف) of as in  Fruit: فاكهة (fakihah = فاكِهَة 

- The #madda  ; meaning extend more, over the ا indicates that the wave extends quite far

- Thefore the ضيا without the hamza represent the transverse wave of light. The #hamza (ء) represent a small amount or a ‘quanta’ as it is the smallest of the Arabic letters and is also pronounced like ‘half alif’. The space between ضيا and ء indicate two separate things, in this case two separate properties of light, namely, the wave and particle nature

- ا is the amplitude, 

- The alif is for اُذُن (= uzun = ear)

- The ا represent the straight light rays
- the Alif with the Hamza (ء) above represent a person or a cause around which something revolves.  Essence center emanate divine power

